{"absent":["Locking or concurrency rules for vdso data, vector selection, vmap or Xen paths.","System call numbers and full register ABI beyond the registers shown.","Layouts of vdso_time_data, vdso_clock, timezone, old timeval, timespec, pt_regs and user_pt_regs.","Behavior when getrandom or clock fallback arguments are invalid or fault.","Branch hardening trampoline code and cross CPU selection policy.","Hypervisor call effects and boot mode recording.","Virtual mapping fault handling and TLB maintenance.","Xen event channel mechanics and inter processor signaling.","Signal stack size value and auxiliary vector delivery.","Hardware capability detection and masking."],"dossier":"D11","findings":[{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/gettimeofday.h::__ASM_VDSO_GETTIMEOFDAY_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/processor.h::__ASM_VDSO_PROCESSOR_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/vsyscall.h::__ASM_VDSO_VSYSCALL_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/vectors.h::__ASM_VECTORS_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/vermagic.h::_ASM_VERMAGIC_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::__ASM__VIRT_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::_ASM_ARM64_VMALLOC_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmap_stack.h::__ASM_VMAP_STACK_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::__ARM64_VNCR_MAPPING_H__","arch/arm64/include/asm/word-at-a-time.h::__ASM_WORD_AT_A_TIME_H","arch/arm64/include/asm/xen/events.h::_ASM_ARM64_XEN_EVENTS_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/auxvec.h::__ASM_AUXVEC_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/bitsperlong.h::__ASM_BITSPERLONG_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/bpf_perf_event.h::_UAPI__ASM_BPF_PERF_EVENT_H__","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/byteorder.h::__ASM_BYTEORDER_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/fcntl.h::__ASM_FCNTL_H","arch/arm64/include/uapi/asm/hwcap.h::_UAPI__ASM_HWCAP_H"],"text":"Examined headers each protect against multiple inclusion with a dedicated guard macro defined once per file."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/getrandom.h::getrandom_syscall"],"text":"User time random helper exposes a direct supervisor request for random bytes. It conveys destination, byte count and flags in the first three argument registers with the getrandom number in the syscall number register, performs a synchronous trap with memory treated as clobbered, and returns the kernel status value."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/gettimeofday.h::gettimeofday_fallback"],"text":"Legacy wall clock fallback exposes a direct supervisor request for time of day. It conveys timeval and timezone pointers in the first two argument registers with the gettimeofday number in the syscall number register, traps synchronously with memory clobbered, and returns the kernel status."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/gettimeofday.h::clock_gettime_fallback","arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/gettimeofday.h::clock_getres_fallback"],"text":"High resolution clock fallbacks expose direct supervisor requests for time and resolution. Both convey clock identifier and timespec pointer in the first two argument registers with their respective clock numbers in the syscall number register, trap synchronously with memory clobbered, and return the kernel status."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/gettimeofday.h::VDSO_HAS_CLOCK_GETRES"],"text":"Virtual dynamic shared object advertises resolution query support with its presence flag set to one."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/gettimeofday.h::__arch_get_hw_counter"],"text":"Hardware counter accessor for virtual clocks returns zero when the mode indicates no usable counter, allowing the generic layer to detect a race with a concurrent update and retry toward a syscall. Otherwise it returns the current virtual count value."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/gettimeofday.h::__arch_get_vdso_u_time_data.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/gettimeofday.h::__arch_get_vdso_u_time_data.alt_2"],"text":"Virtual time data accessor yields the address of the shared user visible time data object while applying a compiler barrier to defeat faulty absolute relocation handling."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/processor.h::cpu_relax"],"text":"Processor relax hint for virtual object spin waits issues a yield indication and orders memory, giving the core a pause opportunity without changing architectural state."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/vsyscall.h::VDSO_PRECISION_MASK"],"text":"Virtual clock precision mask keeps the low fifty six bits set and clears the top eight bits."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/vsyscall.h::__arch_update_vdso_clock.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vdso/vsyscall.h::__arch_update_vdso_clock.alt_2"],"text":"Architecture clock refresh for virtual clocks assigns the precision mask to the clock mask field, constraining readable counter precision."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vectors.h::arm64_bp_harden_el1_vectors"],"text":"Branch hardening vector selector enumerates alternate entry trampolines. It always provides a kernel page table isolation slot and, when branch history mitigation is configured, additionally provides loop, firmware call and clear instruction slots in that order."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vectors.h::EL1_VECTOR_BHB_LOOP","arch/arm64/include/asm/vectors.h::EL1_VECTOR_BHB_FW","arch/arm64/include/asm/vectors.h::EL1_VECTOR_BHB_CLEAR_INSN","arch/arm64/include/asm/vectors.h::TRAMP_VALIAS","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::ARM64_VECTOR_TABLE_LEN"],"text":"When branch history mitigation is disabled the three branch history vector selectors are negative one sentinels. The trampoline alias base is zero and each vector table occupies one SZ_2K granule."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vectors.h::arm64_get_bp_hardening_vector"],"text":"Hardened vector resolver chooses the trampoline alias plus slot stride when the kernel unmapped at exception level zero capability is present, otherwise it uses the direct hardening base plus slot stride. It warns if the isolation slot is requested through the direct path."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vermagic.h::MODULE_ARCH_VERMAGIC"],"text":"Module version magic architecture tag is the string aarch64."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::HVC_SET_VECTORS","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::HVC_SOFT_RESTART","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::HVC_RESET_VECTORS","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::HVC_FINALISE_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::HVC_GET_ICH_VTR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::HVC_STUB_HCALL_NR"],"text":"Hypervisor call function identifiers for early virtualization control are small integers: set vectors zero, soft restart one, reset vectors two, finalise exception level two three, get interrupt controller virtualization table four, and stub handling five."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::HVC_STUB_ERR","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::BOOT_CPU_MODE_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::BOOT_CPU_MODE_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::BOOT_CPU_FLAG_E2H"],"text":"Stub hypervisor error sentinel is hexadecimal badca11. Boot processor mode markers are hexadecimal e11 for exception level one and e12 for exception level two, with an extended host flag occupying bit thirty two."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::is_pkvm_initialized","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::is_hyp_mode_available","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::is_hyp_mode_mismatched"],"text":"Hypervisor availability state derives from recorded boot modes. Protected initialization forces available true and mismatched false. Otherwise available requires both recorded entries to indicate exception level two, and mismatch indicates they differ."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::is_protected_kvm_enabled","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::has_hvhe","arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::is_hyp_nvhe"],"text":"Protected and hypervisor heuristic queries report false inside virtualization host extended code. Outside that context protected mode and host extension reflect their finalized capabilities, while non virtualization host execution requires both hypervisor availability and absence of kernel in hypervisor mode."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/virt.h::pkvm_force_reclaim_guest_page"],"text":"Guest page reclaim forcing query unconditionally reports false in the examined fragment, indicating no forced reclaim."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pud_supported.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pud_supported.alt_2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pmd_supported.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pmd_supported.alt_2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pte_range_map_size.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pte_range_map_size.alt_2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pte_range_unmap_size.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pte_range_unmap_size.alt_2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pte_supported_shift.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pte_supported_shift.alt_2"],"text":"Virtual mapping granularity policy allows page upper directory huge mappings only when section support exists and always allows middle directory mappings. Contiguous page hint mappings require sufficient maximum shift, a range of at least one contiguous run, and natural alignment of both virtual address and physical frame; unmapping distinguishes the contiguous run by the contiguous page flag, and supported shift advertises the contiguous shift for large sizes else page shift."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pgprot_tagged.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vmalloc.h::arch_vmap_pgprot_tagged.alt_2"],"text":"Tagged virtual mapping protection constructor derives a tagged protection value from the supplied protection."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vmap_stack.h::arch_alloc_vmap_stack"],"text":"Kernel stack allocator reserves thread aligned virtual memory on the requested node with thread info allocation flags and caller address tracking, then clears pointer tags before returning the stack base."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_VTTBR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_VTCR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_VMPIDR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_CNTVOFF_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_NVHCR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HSTR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_VPIDR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_TPIDR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HCRX_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_VNCR_EL2"],"text":"Nested virtualization control offsets for early exception level two state are fixed: virtual translation base 0x020, virtual translation control 0x040, virtual affinity 0x050, virtual offset 0x060, nested control 0x078, hypervisor trap 0x080, virtual identifier 0x088, thread pointer 0x090, extended control 0x0A0, and nested base 0x0B0."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_CPACR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_CONTEXTIDR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_SCTLR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ACTLR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_TCR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_AFSR0_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_AFSR1_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ESR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_MAIR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_AMAIR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_MDSCR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_SPSR_EL1"],"text":"Exception level one control offsets are fixed: access control 0x100, context identifier 0x108, system control 0x110, auxiliary control 0x118, translation control 0x120, fault status low 0x128 and high 0x130, exception syndrome 0x138, memory attribute 0x140, auxiliary attribute 0x148, debug control 0x158, and saved status 0x160."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_CNTV_CVAL_EL0","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_CNTV_CTL_EL0","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_CNTP_CVAL_EL0","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_CNTP_CTL_EL0","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_SCXTNUM_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_TFSR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HDFGRTR2_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HDFGWTR2_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HFGRTR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HFGWTR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HFGITR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HDFGRTR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HDFGWTR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ZCR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HAFGRTR_EL2"],"text":"Timer, thread and fine trap offsets are fixed: virtual timer compare 0x168 and control 0x170, physical timer compare 0x178 and control 0x180, thread number 0x188, tag fault status 0x190, debug trap second read 0x1A0 write 0x1B0, general trap read 0x1B8 write 0x1C0 inject 0x1C8, debug trap read 0x1D0 write 0x1D8, vector length 0x1E0, and alternate trap read 0x1E8."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_TTBR0_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_TTBR1_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_FAR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ELR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_SP_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_VBAR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_TCR2_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_SCTLR2_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PIRE0_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PIR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_POR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HFGRTR2_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HFGWTR2_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_HFGITR2_EL2"],"text":"Translation, exception and permission offsets are fixed: translation bases 0x200 and 0x210, fault address 0x220, exception link 0x230, stack pointer 0x240, vector base 0x250, second translation control 0x270, second system control 0x278, indirect zero 0x290, indirect 0x2A0, overlay 0x2A8, second trap read 0x2C0 write 0x2C8, and second inject 0x310."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR0_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR1_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR2_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR3_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR4_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR5_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR6_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR7_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR8_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR9_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR10_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR11_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR12_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR13_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR14_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_LR15_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_AP0R0_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_AP0R1_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_AP0R2_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_AP0R3_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_AP1R0_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_AP1R1_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_AP1R2_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_AP1R3_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_HCR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_VMCR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_VDISR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_VSESR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_HFGITR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_HFGRTR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_ICH_HFGWTR_EL2"],"text":"Interrupt virtualization offsets use eight byte strides: list registers zero through fifteen span 0x400 to 0x478, active priority groups span 0x480 to 0x498 and 0x4A0 to 0x4B8, hypervisor control 0x4C0, virtual control 0x4C8, deferred interrupt 0x500, system error 0x508, plus fine trap inject 0xB10 read 0xB18 write 0xB20."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMBLIMITR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMBPTR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMBSR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMSCR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMSEVFR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMSICR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMSIRR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMSLATFR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMSNEVFR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_PMSDSFR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_TRFCR_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_MPAM1_EL1","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_MPAMHCR_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_MPAMVPMV_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_MPAMVPM0_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_MPAMVPM1_EL2","arch/arm64/include/asm/vncr_mapping.h::VNCR_